; SIGNATURE PROBE at (-> (List a) (List a)) — the shape the reversal need has.
;
; The law is reflexive and therefore states nothing: no definition in the corpus
; carries it, so --spec cannot match it and falls through to LISTING every
; definition whose signature is compatible. That fallback list is the point. It
; answers "what does this corpus hold at this shape?" before any real law is
; written, and it prints each candidate's GUARANTEE — which is how the falsified
; twin announces itself.
(defn wanted [a] [(xs (List a))] (List a)
  (prop refl [(xs (List Int))]
    (== (wanted [Int] xs) (wanted [Int] xs))))
